3. How They Fit Together in .NETUnderstanding how these three layers interact provides a clear mental model of modern software development[cite: 1]:Platform (.NET): Provides the runtime engine (CLR), garbage collector, JIT compiler, and the CLI to execute applications on Windows, Linux, or macOS[cite: 1].
Framework (ASP.NET Core / WPF): Sits on top of the platform, providing the structural rules, routing, and lifecycle management for your application type[cite: 1].
Library (Newtonsoft.Json / Custom Class Library): Integrated into your application to handle specific features like serialization, logging, or mathematics[cite: 1].
4. Key TakeawaysInversion of Control (IoC) is the defining technical distinction between a library and a framework[cite: 1].
You call a Library; a Framework calls you; a Platform runs everything[cite: 1].
C# is the programming language, .NET is the Platform, ASP.NET Core is a Framework, and tools like Dapper are Libraries[cite: 1].
